<title>CANADA: Ontario Pork eyes Manitoba Pork forward contracts.</title>
<headline>Ontario Pork eyes Manitoba Pork forward contracts.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ontario's single-desk hog marketer said Tuesday it may offer a forward contract program to farmers similar to that designed by Manitoba Pork.</p>
<p>&quot;We are looking at a program similar to Manitoba Pork's. Manitoba has developed a program that's very effective and that's why we're in discussion with Manitoba Pork,&quot; Ontario Pork communications director Mary Lou McLeod told Reuters.</p>
<p>Ontario farmers produced 3.7 million hogs in calendar 1995 while Toronto-based Ontario Pork exported an average 10,000 hogs each week, McLeod said.</p>
<p>The agency currently runs auctions and offers spot contracts.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
